  "description": "Prior Approval in relation to the erection of 2 new floors to provide 30 self contained residential units and an additional refuse store, cycle store and parking.",
  "subdivision_of_building": null,
  "actual_completion_date": null,
  "lpa_app_no": "DM2025/00793",
  "decision": "Approved",
  "application_type_full": "Prior Approval: New dwellinghouses on detached buildings in commercial or mixed use",
  "last_updated_by": "Idox Uniform",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "id": "Sutton-DM2025_00793",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Prior to the commencement of the development (excluding demolition works), full details of the secure cycle storage facilities shall be submitted to, and approved in writing by, the Local Planning Authority which shall show their positioning within the site, the size and materials of the enclosure and the means of access. The approved details shall be implemented on site prior to the first occupation of the development hereby approved and thereafter permanently retained in accordance with the approved details.\r\rReason: To ensure the development provides an adequate level of cycle parking facilities and to encourage sustainable modes of transport, in accordance with Policies 36 and 37 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018. This condition is required to be pre-commencement as cycle storage needs to be designed into the scheme at a early stage of the construction process and respect the materials and design of the development.",
    "All external facing materials, treatments and finishes shall be similar to those of the original building and maintained and retained thereafter. This applies unless differences are shown on the drawings we have approved. \r\rReason: To ensure that the extension harmonises with the existing building and to ensure compliance with Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "Any vehicle parked on the garage forecourt should not be allowed to overhang the highway boundary as to do so without lawful authority may be an offence against section 137 of the Highway Act 1980.",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) - Schedule 2, Part 20, Class AA.",
    "Prior approval is required and granted  Under, Schedule 2, Part 20, Class AA (new dwellinghouses on detached buildings in commercial or mixed use) of The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) to assess:\r1. The transport and highways impacts of the development, \r2. Air traffic and defence asset impacts of the development\r3. Contamination risks in relation to the building\r4. Flooding risks\r5. The external appearance of the building\r6.The provision of adequate natural light in all habitable rooms of the dwellinghouses\r7. the impact on the amenity of the existing building and neighbouring premises including overlooking, privacy and the loss of light\r8. The impacts of noise from any commercial premises on the intended occupiers of the new dwellinghouses\r9. The  impacts of the introduction of, or an increase in, a residential use of premises in the area on the carrying on of any trade, business or other use of land in the area;\r10. Whether, because of the siting of the building, the development will impact on a protected view identified in the Directions Relating to Protected Vistas dated 15th March 2012(a) issued by the Secretary of State, and the provisions of paragraph B (prior approval) of this Part apply in relation to that application.\r11. Where the existing building is 18 metres or more in height, the fire safety of the external wall construction of the existing building, and the provisions of paragraph B (prior approval) of this Part apply in relation to that application.\r12. Where the development meets the fire risk condition (see paragraph C(3) of this Part), the fire safety impacts on the intended occupants of the building.}\r13. Meets internal space standards.",
    "Following occupation of the development hereby approved, every dwellinghouse in the building must remain in use as a dwellinghouse within the meaning of Class C3 of the Schedule to the Use Classes Order and for no other purpose, except to the extent that the other purpose is ancillary to the primary use as a dwellinghouse. \r\rReason: To comply with the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) - Schedule 2, Part 20, Class AA,  A.A2 (7).",
    "The site and building works required to implement the development shall be only carried out between the hours of 08:00 and 18:00 Mondays to Fridays and between 08:00 and 13:00 on Saturdays and not at all on Bank Holidays and Sundays\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the neighbours by minimising impacts of the development that would otherwise give rise to nuisance and to ensure compliance with Policies 29 and 34 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "Prior to the occupation of the development the final details of the Electric Vehicle Charging (EVC) points shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The details shall include the location of the 3 active EVC charging points.\r\rReason: To improve air quality and provide ECV infrastructure in accordance with policies 34 and 37 of the Sutton Local Plan.",
    "The fourth floor balustrade on the north-west and north-east facing elevations (serving flats 27, 28 , 29 and 30 as per drawing no. 24.1503/206 F) of the development hereby approved shall be glazed with obscure glass and retained thereafter.\r\rReason: To safeguard the current level of privacy enjoyed by the occupants of adjoining properties in accordance with policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018."
  ],
